{"analysis": "None of the 8 combinations of weight ordering (b-before-w vs w-before-b), transposition, and head layout produced coherent output. The issue is more subtle. I need to check intermediate values within a single layer to pinpoint exactly where the forward pass diverges — is it the attention path, the MLP path, or both?",
  "plan": "Write a debug program that processes token 464 ("The") through layer 0 only, printing the L2 norm at each sub-step (after LN_1, after QKV projection, after attention output, after c_proj, after residual, after LN_2, after c_fc, after gelu, after c_proj, after MLP residual). This will show which component produces unreasonable values.",
